Yes. With `[userId]`, the effect runs on mount and every time userId changes, which is what you want so the list updates when the user changes.

```js
useEffect(() => {
  let ignore = false;
  fetch(`/api/users/${userId}/items`)
    .then(r => r.json())
    .then(data => { if (!ignore) setItems(data); });
  return () => { ignore = true; };
}, [userId]);
```

The `ignore` flag in the cleanup stops an old response from overwriting a newer one if userId changes quickly.
